# Pinned FFmpeg/ffprobe for ClipHack (arm64 macOS).
#
# Audio-only LGPL build, produced from source by THIS project's
# scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh and published in ClipHack's own releases repo. Both
# halves matter: the recipe is ours (so we can supply Corresponding Source for
# exactly what we ship), and the hosting is ours (pruning in WaxOnWaxOff already
# deleted a deps release out from under us during its v2.0.6 cut, which broke
# building from a clean checkout until it was noticed).
#
# Configured with NO --enable-gpl, NO --enable-nonfree, NO --enable-version3, and
# no video or image external libraries; libmp3lame (LAME 3.100) is the only
# external library.
#
# REPRODUCIBLE: `./scripts/build-ffmpeg.sh <dir>` on the same toolchain rebuilds
# these byte for byte, so the checksums below are independently verifiable rather
# than merely asserted.
#
# r4 keeps LC_UUID. r2 dropped it for reproducibility, and dyld on macOS 26.7
# refuses to load an executable without one, so every r2 binary aborts there.
# r3 (2026-09-16) put LC_UUID back but was not reproducible — rebuilding its
# recipe changed the UUID and the signature hash over it, 48 bytes in all. r4
# is r3's machine code, byte for byte outside those 48 bytes, from a recipe that
# gets reproducibility from ZERO_AR_DATE instead. Built with Xcode 27.
# The suffix is the recipe revision: 8.0.3-r4 is the r4 recipe pinned to
# FFmpeg 8.0.3, the third point release on the 8.0 branch.
#
# Superseded pins must NOT be deleted — each is what older tags verify against,
# and removing one makes those tags unbuildable from a clean checkout:
#   ffmpeg-deps-8.0-audio-arm64      v1.17.0            (byte-identical mirrors
#                                                        of the WaxOnWaxOff build)
#   ffmpeg-deps-8.0-audio-arm64-r2   v1.17.1 – v1.25.2
#   ffmpeg-deps-8.0-audio-arm64-r3   v1.25.3, and WaxOnWaxOff v2.12.2 and
#                                    FilmStrip v1.9.2, which borrowed it
#   ffmpeg-deps-8.0-audio-arm64-r4   v1.25.4 – v1.25.8
#
# LICENSE: FFmpeg 8.0.3 core is LGPL-2.1-or-later, LAME is LGPL-2.0-or-later, and
# the arnndn filter is BSD-2-Clause. No GPL-licensed components are compiled in.
# Verify after any pin change with `./ClipHackKit/ffmpeg -version` — the
# configure line must not contain --enable-gpl.
#
# This replaces ffmpeg-deps-8.0-arm64, a third-party GPL build (OSXExperts.NET,
# linking x264/x265/libvidstab) whose release assets no longer exist.
FFMPEG_VERSION=8.0.3
FFMPEG_ARCH=arm64
# The deps release MUST stay flagged as a prerelease. It shares a repo with the
# app DMGs, and GitHub resolves /releases/latest by date — an ordinary release
# here becomes "latest" and breaks the README download link
# (/releases/latest/download/ClipHack-vX.Y.Z.dmg) until it is reflagged. The
# in-app updater is unaffected either way; it filters for ^v[0-9] tags.
FFMPEG_DEPS_REPO=sevmorris/ClipHack-releases
FFMPEG_DEPS_TAG=ffmpeg-deps-8.0.3-audio-arm64-r4
FFMPEG_SHA256=2f81b39303379a48839197eff1d2fb4fb8d31aab1258806290e4eb052f20613c
FFPROBE_SHA256=67442cbc4cab95b846f44b379db5655e751de5b99d6ffbe0500073e41e2a520c

# Corresponding upstream source (LGPL §6).
FFMPEG_SOURCE_RELEASE=8.0.3
FFMPEG_SOURCE_RELEASE_DATE=2026-06-18
FFMPEG_SOURCE_ARCHIVE=ffmpeg-8.0.3.tar.xz
FFMPEG_SOURCE_URL=https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.0.3.tar.xz
FFMPEG_SOURCE_SIGNATURE_URL=https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.0.3.tar.xz.asc
FFMPEG_SOURCE_GIT_TAG=n8.0.3
LAME_SOURCE_URL=https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/lame/lame/3.100/lame-3.100.tar.gz
